We establish the equilibrium conditions for the $j$-unit analytical discrete model by evaluating the stationary points of the total potential energy. With the prescribed vertical displacement \(u\), the reaction force \(F\) arises in response to the displacement. This response allows the angular inclination \(\alpha\) to adjust freely, ensuring the system reaches angular equilibrium and minimizes potential energy. Specifically, we determine the system's equilibrium using the following equations (see Supplemental
Material~\cite{SI} for the detailed derivation):
\begin{equation}\label{Eq:eq5}
\frac{\partial E_j}{\partial u} = F, \quad \frac{\partial E_j}{\partial \alpha} = 0 \quad \text{for} \; j = 1, 2, \ldots, N
\end{equation}
