Next is the “No Switch" variant, which yielded a win rate of 58.8\%. Note that in this condition, only strategic switching is disabled; the AI may still switch Pokémon if one faints. The significant performance drop highlights the model's ability to engage in forward planning and select the optimal Pokémon for each situation.

Finally, the “No Item” variant performed the worst, with an average win rate of only 32.6\%. This result aligns with expectations, as removing the five healing potions severely handicaps the agent's ability to sustain its team during extended combat.


